        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>compacted_data_size</name>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Min size of disk space required to store data of all spaces of the database. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>In other words, the size of disk space the database would occupy if all spaces were compacted and there were no indexes. Accounted in bytes, without taking into account disk compression. Estimated as the size of data stored in the last level of primary LSM trees. Along with disk_data_size and disk_index_size, it can be used for evaluating space amplification. </para>        </detaileddescription>
